From bebe81fbb2f6abd46e8988887ed836ef4d1eaa66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 09:31:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: dsi: force command mode in mtk_dsi_poweron()

mtk_dsi_reset_engine() does not touch DSI_MODE_CTRL, so whatever the
bootloader left there survives power-on. On boards where the bootloader
lights the panel for a boot logo and hands the DSI over still running, the
leftover value is a video mode, and the first mtk_dsi_host_transfer() then
takes the "already streaming" path: it stops the stream and waits for
VM_DONE, which never arrives because nothing is actually being scanned out.
The panel's very first command fails and it is never initialised:

  [drm] Wait DSI IRQ(0x00000008) Timeout
  *ERROR* failed to switch cmd mode
  sending dcs data 8f a5 failed: -62

Write CMD_MODE to DSI_MODE_CTRL right after the engine reset. Command mode
is the correct state to power on into regardless of what came before; the
video mode is programmed by mtk_dsi_start() when the stream is actually
started, exactly as today.

Seen on the Amazon Fire HD 10 (2017), whose LK bootloader draws its logo
over DSI in video mode and never stops the stream before jumping to the
kernel.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
index 49dfc0f82..7b08a212a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
@@ -737,6 +737,29 @@ static int mtk_dsi_poweron(struct mtk_dsi *dsi)
 		       dsi->regs + dsi->driver_data->reg_shadow_dbg_off);
 
 	mtk_dsi_reset_engine(dsi);
+
+	/*
+	 * Force command mode before anything can try to send a DCS command.
+	 *
+	 * mtk_dsi_reset_engine() does not touch DSI_MODE_CTRL, so whatever the
+	 * bootloader left there survives. On boards where the bootloader lights
+	 * the panel for a boot logo and hands it over still running -- the
+	 * Amazon Fire HD 10 does exactly this -- that leftover value is a video
+	 * mode, and the first mtk_dsi_host_transfer() takes the "already
+	 * streaming" path: it stops the stream and waits for VM_DONE, which
+	 * never arrives because nothing is actually being scanned out. The
+	 * panel's very first command then fails and it is never initialised:
+	 *
+	 *   [drm] Wait DSI IRQ(0x00000008) Timeout
+	 *   *ERROR* failed to switch cmd mode
+	 *   sending dcs data 8f a5 failed: -62
+	 *
+	 * Command mode is the right state to power on into regardless; video
+	 * mode is programmed by mtk_dsi_start() when the stream actually
+	 * starts.
+	 */
+	writel(CMD_MODE, dsi->regs + DSI_MODE_CTRL);
+
 	mtk_dsi_phy_timconfig(dsi);
 
 	mtk_dsi_ps_control(dsi, true);
